WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.311
Week 6: The Present: Regular Actions. describe habits ask about routines say how often something happens

2
00:00:07.311 --> 00:00:14.815
Cultural lens. Daily schedules and meal times differ across regions and urban/rural contexts.

3
00:00:14.815 --> 00:00:26.886
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:26.886 --> 00:00:38.744
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:38.744 --> 00:00:47.743
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:47.743 --> 00:01:19.740
Model language. El horario laboral cambia según el país. — The work schedule changes by country. La comida principal no siempre es al mediodía. — The main meal is not always at midday. Las costumbres varían entre zonas rurales y urbanas. — Customs vary between rural and urban areas. Muchas familias comparten la cena. — Many families share dinner. El contexto determina el horario de cada persona. — Context determines each person's schedule.

7
00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:29.659
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
